This README file contains a brief description of the verification case.

This is a integrated test for the gap and also the gaps behavior for TRISO. The
geometry is like:

          Kernel                      Buffer             IPyC     SiC     OPyC
------------------------------x------------------|    |--------x-------x--------
                             250                350  360      400     435     475um

Other input parameters:
- wedgeAngle: 2 degrees;
- Buffer porosity: 0.4054;
- Heat source : 3.2e9 W/m³;
- Time:  1e7s;
- Roughness: 1e-6 m, 2e-6 m;


The following items have been verified:
- The volume of the gap;
- The volume of the gas in the Buffer;
- The production of CO;
- The gas pressure;


=============================== Volume of the gap ===============================

The volume of the gap should be:
Vgap = 4/3*pi*(360³-350³)*1e-18 = 1.58378157642973E-11

In the offbeat model, the wedge angel is 2 degrees, so the fraction of the model is:
fraction = (2/180*pi)²/4/pi = 9.69627362219072E-05

So the real volume is  Vgap*fraction = 1.53567795228473E-15

And the volume calculated by OFFBEAT is 1.53459e-15

The relative error is 0.0708450807090187%

========================== Volume of the gas in the Buffer ========================

In order to have the volume of Buffer, a faceZone is created between Kernel and
Buffer. So we need to test the correctness of the volume calculated with a faceZone
and a patch(bufferOuter).

The gas volume should be:
4/3*pi*(350³-250³)*1e-18*fraction*porosity = 4.48687243866232E-15

The volume by OFFBEAT is 4.48368e-15

The relative error is 0.0711506445961727%

============================= Production of CO ==================================

--------- GA model ----------------------------

The calculated Kernel outer T is 1321.9505615234375 K

So the production rate is :
COprod = 1.64*exp(-3311/T) = 0.133997250066855 atom/fission

The fission rate is:
fission_rate = (3.2e9 W/m³ / 3.2e-11 J/fission) = 1e20 fission/s/m³

the total fission is :
fission = fission_rate * 4/3*pi*250³*1e-18*fraction * 1e7 = 6346196245556.43

The total CO produced in kg is:
Mass_CO = COprod * fission /AvogadrosNumber * 28.01 / 1000 = 3.95522860487728E-14

The OFFBEAT value is 3.95245e-14

The relative error is 0.0702514356275999%

--------- Proksch model ----------------------------

Instead of Kernel outer temperature, Proksch use the time average time
integrated surface temperature of the TRISO particle. In this case, it is set as
a boundary condtion of 1273 K.

Similar to GA model, the prodcution rate is :
COprod = (1e7)²/(1.211e10*10.0^(8500.0/1273)) = 0.00173666177031998 atom/fission

The total CO produced in kg is:
Mass_CO = COprod * fission /AvogadrosNumber * 28.01 / 1000 = 5.12614572876632E-16

The OFFBEAT value is 5.12E-16

The relative error is 0.0709251932872769%

=============================== Gas pressure ===================================

From calculation, we know the average temperature of gap gas is 1293.3 K, the average
Buffer gas temperature is 1310.33.

So the pressure should be: (using Proksch model)
P = Mass_CO / 28.01 * 1000 * R / (1.53567795228473E-15/1293.3 + 4.48687243866232E-15/1310.33)
  = 32993.799923485 Pa

The OFFBEAT value is 32997

The relative error is 0.00969902382393587%
